# The parity corpus is compared byte for byte, so git must not rewrite any of
# it on checkout. On Windows, `core.autocrlf=true` is the default from Git for
# Windows' installer, and it converts every LF in these files to CRLF -- after
# which the binary (Rust's `writeln!` emits LF on every platform) differs from
# its own reference on every single line, for a reason that has nothing to do
# with the port. `-text` disables that conversion in both directions.
#
# Not theoretical: without this, `cargo test` on a Windows runner fails
# `config_write::tests::generated_default_config_matches_the_committed_python_oracle`,
# because that test `include_str!`s parity/references/generated_config_v2.2.0.ini
# and compares it to generated text. It blocked the v2.2.1 release build.
parity/references/**   -text
parity/fixtures/**     -text
parity/golden_config.ini -text

# Truncated FITS and XISF frames: real binary content, never line-ending
# material, and not worth attempting to diff as text.
parity/fixtures/binary/**  binary
